    "narrative": "The offensive core for Ghost Ride the WHIP centers on the elite matchup for **Corbin Carroll**, whose 87.14 projection is the clear ceiling play of the day. Facing a soft xERA of 4.80, **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a slow opposing pitcher delivery that boosts his high-value stolen base potential, paired with a strong 0.376 xwOBA. Joining him in the \"Strong\" tier is **Tyler Soderstrom** (73.03), who leverages a favorable park and high-upside matchup against a vulnerable arm. **Mickey Moniak** also demands attention at the UTIL slot; while his matchup against a moderate-skill arm is balanced, his 14% platoon boost makes him an efficient engine for run production today. \n\nThe lineup construction is defensive against high-end pitching but aggressive on platoons. The most difficult personnel decision involved **Vinnie Pasquantino**, who finished just outside the starting nine with a 50.88 score. While his 14% dynamic platoon boost was enticing, the optimizer ultimately pivoted to **Zach McKinstry** (52.41) and **Henry Bolte** (51.94) due to their superior positional utility and superior matchups against high-xERA starters. **Seiya Suzuki** remains a volatile but necessary start (67.03), though he carries a specific risk profile today; while his matchup is strong, the wind blowing in forces a 5% penalty to his output, requiring a watchful eye as lineups materialize. \n\nManagers should remain alert regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" status for the entire roster. While these projections assume specific batting orders, a drop in the order for **Brice Turang** or **Cole Young** could trigger a re-evaluation of their 50\u201358 range scores. We are avoiding the sub-40 danger zone with **Dalton Rushing** and **Carson Williams** on the bench, ensuring we preserve our limited game caps for the favorable conditions surrounding **Austin Riley** (67.09) and **Gabriel Moreno** (65.19). Trust the platoon leverage, but monitor the wind in the **Seiya Suzuki** game closely.",
